"Viv was born Viviane Saint-Lys in Nice, France, on Earth; con-artist forebears made up the name."
"On Earth Viv was a corporal and combat medic of the French army, in Afghanistan and Mali."
"The god Emeric took Viv's Earth body to flee his wife Maranor, and her soul was flung to Nyil."
"Emeric left a divine spark of luck in Viv; it became her Will of the Black Witch."
"Emeric lived on Earth as Viv, married, had three children; her father learned it and died."
"Emeric took Viv's fertility; she can bear no children."
"Viv left a younger brother, Damien, and friends Mouq and Gevaudan on Earth, never to see them again."
"Viv swore to the gods never to tell that every god was once a mortal human."
"Viv knows Maradoc pushed Maranor through a portal to Earth at Mornyr."
"Viv knows Emeric came back from Earth disguised as an aged Viv, and holds the gods' throne again."
"Viv holds the Master Core, a self-renewing core of every hue, kept secret at Judgment's urging."
"Solfis's flying fortress was built from the Chalice, the floating isle Harrak stole from Helock."
"Viv keeps a hidden second web of portals, the Ghost Network, even inside allied Baran."
"Viv hid a kill switch under every portal gate she built."
"Viv hid an orphan with one of Avarice's hatchlings, to avenge her should she fall."
"Viv confessed to Neriad's High Inquisitor that she murdered a bishop of Neriad."
"Viv murdered Constable Tarano during a truce talk."
"Worship is pouring into Viv under the attributes Order, Change and Progress."
"Viv's ascension to godhood is delayed; she will stay weak for decades."
"Viv will one day become a god."
"Viv will one day sail west on the Voyager, seeking a land beyond the Endless Sea."
